refactor/split-utilities

PURPOSE: 
Split utilities.py into a more manageable collection of files to increase 
readability as well as identify opportunities for extensibility more easily.
These files are housed in ./src/ and should not contain any user entry points.

Currently, new code tends to get added to the top of the file, resulting in 
messy organization. The goal is that new code should be added in 
src/my_code.py and imported as necessary. 

The goal of this branch is NOT to refactor existing code. 
Helper functions are being created to remove duplicate code. Names
are changed to clarify purpose or conform with style guides. Type hints are 
used as much as possible. Deprecated notation has been modernized. Comments 
and docstrings are largely removed in favor of self-explaining code.

Notes indicating specific areas for future refactoring efforts are indicated
by `# [!]`. These are sometimes meandering thoughts or questions. They should 
be removed prior to the PR. 

DISCLAIMER: 
I used AI assistance for this. All of the code was typed by hand (even the 
code directly copied from utilities.py) to help me better understand the
project as a whole. ChatGPT was primarily used to assist with naming 
conventions and identifying modernization methods. We had a riveting
discussion on what to name the Paths class, whether it should even be a 
class, and what the scope of its content should be. Super exciting stuff.

